  "acceptance": {
    "workflow": "Explicit local operator certification and JSON CLI inspection of a captured static Docker/XFS profile; existing providers opt into requiring a current report.",
    "contract": "Optional host-certification module, certifyLinuxHost, inspectLinuxHostCertification and requireCurrentLinuxHostCertification. Seven fixed capabilities; immutable clank-linux-host-certification/1 reports, private local HMAC authentication and bounded reason codes.",
    "binding": "Fresh boot/kernel/architecture, process identity/capabilities, namespace/forwarding settings, selected mount identity/options, all framework JavaScript/runtime bytes, enforcement-tool content/permissions and local daemon/resolved immutable image identity. Policy and wall/boot uptime expiry rechecked at inspection; report snapshot rechecked after host sampling.",
    "enforcement": "Actual isolated successful/rejected migrations, terminated endless SQL and atomic rollback/recovery; mapped user/mount/network namespaces; selected byte/inode and SQLite/WAL quota denial with outside controls; production non-root Docker launcher, exact selected memory/swap/CPU/PID values, read-only root/code, absent host secret, zero capabilities/no-new-privileges and bounded tmpfs.",
    "egress": "Controlled private namespace endpoints prove routing before policy for allowed/denied/public/private/metadata and host destinations. Selected Docker/nft policy then admits only the representative allowed address and matching pinned name; deny-all profile separately passes. No requests reach real external control addresses.",
    "failure": "Real namespace denial, missing immutable image, killed parent during an active SQLite transaction, and nft execution denial during cleanup all prevent green. Killed worker exits and pending data/ledger roll back. Denied cleanup retains both markers until exact ownership-verified manual cleanup.",
    "persistence": "Private owned key/report/attempt metadata, pinned no-symlink directory and no-follow bounded reads, exclusive per-directory/root-host attempts. Keys/reports fsynced, report atomically renamed and directory synced. Earlier report invalidated before probing; incomplete attempts remain blocked. Detached CLI/process inspection recovers a completed result.",
    "compatibility": "No application or provider-store migration, new dependency, automatic image pull, remote inherited Docker context, caller probe callback, arbitrary executable or process-runner fallback. New optional JS/declaration pair explicitly raises only the file ceiling from 401 to 403; byte ceiling remains 6 MiB."
  },
