  "reviewFixes": [
    "Decode module URLs correctly for installations containing spaces.",
    "Require exact Docker memory/swap/CPU/PID values rather than merely positive limits.",
    "Force the local Unix Docker daemon and a private clean launcher context.",
    "Boundly wait for XFS delayed deallocation; never clear a quota with outstanding usage.",
    "Retain attempt markers on uncertain final cleanup and verify potentially uncertain routes/links.",
    "Use deferred imports inside the embedded runner to preserve the browser import contract.",
    "Fsync private keys/reports and the publication directory; verify current report bytes and expiry after fresh host sampling."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "V1 static isolated-Docker profiles only; 4\u201364 MiB aligned persistent quota and 32\u2013128 inode limits, 128 MiB\u20132 GiB container memory, 0.1\u20134 CPUs and 16\u201332768 PIDs. Larger/different policies cannot reuse this certificate.",
    "Controlled representative allowed/denied IPv4 addresses and selected pinned names are sampled; universal public allow policies without a denied-public control are unsupported. External availability/DNS and every possible exhaustion behavior are not attested.",
    "Certification is an expiring point-in-time measurement, not continuous monitoring or protection from a compromised host operator. Arbitrary external policy-file changes are not attested.",
    "Forced crash cleanup is explicit operator work; no age-based automatic unlock or recycled live quota assignment. A running SQLite task settles or hits its fixed deadline before cancellation cleanup.",
    "No production Railway certificate, production deployment, provider leadership/failover/handoff, fleet simulation or remote PITR acceptance is claimed. The existing ordinary gate still has its three privileged skips; the real guest suite separately runs with zero skips."
  ],
